  "caveats": [
    "Per-nucleon NF shifts (shift_p_h3=19, shift_n_h3=15) are the H_3-context standalone values; the per-NEW-nucleon embedded values in the (18, 21) decomposition come from prop:per-nucleon-shift-additive-linearity (already proven and verified at A=2..6).",
    "LP active-set is a DISCRETE invariant (the cardinality of {i : y_i^* > 0}) — robust to ~1e-9 float jitter. Scipy linprog (f64) is used as the discrete oracle; every numerical value in the witness is recomputed in mpmath at the requested dps precision via a high-precision linear solve restricted to the active basis.",
    "The shift_NF symbolic-q computation (build_atom_nf_sym in hecke_core_symbolic) is intractably slow at A≥2 due to expression fan-out across ~25 hm_sym ops × 6 NF entries without intermediate canonicalization. A principled fix routes the shift through the crystal-bases pole-order reading (prop:crystal-pole-order), where the q → 0 Kashiwara crystal collapses fan-out to monomial actions. Pending follow-up; for this witness the shift is read from the closed form 18Z + 21N + 1."
  ]
